---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import scenes from '../../data/scenes.json';
import contributors from '../../data/contributors.json';
const open = scenes.scenes.filter((s) => s.status === 'open');
const repo = 'https://github.com/Ivan666jjj/yuanmingyuan-restoration';
---
<Base lang="en" title="Contribute · Yuanmingyuan Restoration">
  <div class="page-head"><div class="wrap row">
    <div><p class="kicker">OPEN CALL</p><h1>Contribute</h1></div>
    <p>No coding required. Any AI image tool will do: submit one image, one prompt, one source, and a scene returns to the map.</p>
  </div></div>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents"><a href="#how">How</a><a href="#spec">Checklist</a><a href="#three-d">3D</a><a href="#list">To claim</a><a href="#wall">Contributors</a></nav>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="how">How</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><b>Claim</b>: open a <a href={`${repo}/issues/new?template=claim-scene.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">claim issue</a>, or click a hollow dot on the map.</li>
        <li><b>Research</b>: find references (copperplates, album, old photos, Lei drawings) per the scene's listed basis.</li>
        <li><b>Make</b>: write parameter-rich prompts, generate with references, self-check the physics list.</li>
        <li><b>Submit</b>: attach image + metadata to the issue; Git users open a PR, others we merge for you.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="spec">Checklist</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Image: 2940×1912 PNG or WebP ≥1600px.</li>
        <li>Reference source: link or holding info, public domain or licensed.</li>
        <li>Full prompt + model name/version.</li>
        <li>One line: what is sourced, what is inferred.</li>
        <li>Credit: your name/ID for the contributor wall.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="note">Rules: no fabricated “sources”; never present AI images as photographs or surveys; references must be traceable; images shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.</div>
      <h2 id="three-d">Three-dimensional restorations</h2>
      <p>Blender, SketchUp or scripted modelling — all welcome. 3D ranks equal to images: <b>renders alone count</b>; add a glb and the scene becomes rotatable in the gallery and viewable in AR on a phone.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>One hero render plus front, side and oblique views, WebP ≥1600px.</li>
        <li>Optional glb, ≤10MB; metres, origin at terrace centre, Y-up. Trim geometry first — Draco shifts decoding to an overseas CDN.</li>
        <li>State element by element what is sourced and what is estimated.</li>
        <li>Procedural or public-domain textures only; no unverified scans or images from the web.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="note">3D is checkable geometry, not a survey. It stands only if the column grid, bays and dimensions trace back to the drawings; materials and painted decoration remain inference and must be labelled.</div>
      <p class="small"><a href={`${repo}/issues/new?template=submit-3d.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Submit 3D →</a>　Spec in <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">CONTRIBUTING</a></p>
      <h2 id="list">Scenes to claim ({open.length})</h2>
      <div class="claim-list">
        {open.map((s, i) => (
          <div class="row">
            <span class="idx">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <h3>{s.en}</h3>
            <span class="r">{s.garden} · {s.ref}</span>
            <a href={`${repo}/issues/new?template=claim-scene.yml&title=${encodeURIComponent('Claim: ' + s.en)}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Claim</a>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h2 id="wall">Contributors</h2>
      <p class="small">Everyone whose submission is accepted stays here. Restore a piece, sign a piece.</p>
      <div class="claim-list" style="border-top:1px solid var(--ink)">
        {contributors.map((c, i) => (
          <div class="row"><span class="idx">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{c.name}</h3><span class="r">{c.scenes} scenes · {c.role}</span><a href={c.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Profile</a></div>
        ))}
        <div class="row"><span class="idx">＋</span><h3 style="color:var(--muted)">Your name here</h3><span class="r">The next piece might be yours</span><a href={`${repo}/issues/new?template=claim-scene.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>